# Defense-in-depth ignores for the mobile tree.
#
# The Flutter-generated `android/.gitignore` per app already covers
# `key.properties`, `**/*.keystore`, and `**/*.jks`, plus most build artefacts;
# this file is the workspace-level safety net so a stray drop at the canonical
# Firebase / signing paths is *physically* impossible to commit by accident.
#
# `*.example` placeholders are intentionally NOT ignored — they document the
# expected file layout and are safe to track.

# --- Firebase config (real files only; .example files stay tracked) ---
**/google-services.json
!**/google-services.json.example
**/GoogleService-Info.plist
!**/GoogleService-Info.plist.example

# --- Android signing material (belt-and-braces; per-app android/.gitignore already covers these) ---
**/key.properties
!**/key.properties.example
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/*.kdb
**/keystore/

# --- Apple signing material (never enters the repo) ---
**/*.p8
**/*.p12
**/*.mobileprovision
**/*.cer

# --- Generic env / secret droppings ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/secrets/
